From 2eb0884196b31b2366480be2eb62c78f09433cda Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: jarojarojaro-jaro <miki.jaroszek@gmail.com>
Date: Tue, 13 Oct 2026 15:25:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 29/65] ggml-backend/llama: asynchronous graph input uploads
 (LLAMA_ASYNC_INPUTS)

Each host-resident split input was copied with a blocking copy: a sync of the
split backend's stream, then cudaMemcpyAsync + cudaStreamSynchronize on the
per-thread stream. That is ~22 us of GPU idle per input on gfx1100 and 16
inputs per speculative step (8 verify, 4 MTP catch-up, 4 MTP draft chain).

- sched: with ggml_backend_sched_set_async_inputs() host inputs are uploaded
  with set_tensor_async on the split backend's stream (ordered before the
  split's graph); an event recorded after the uploads is waited for in
  ggml_backend_sched_wait_inputs() before host input memory is written again
  (llama: before set_inputs; sched: reset/alloc/compute/free).
- sched: ggml_backend_sched_set_tensor_async() for device-resident inputs
  (the MTP draft chain pins its inputs to the GPU): pinned staging memory,
  async upload; the llama input setters go through llm_graph_input_set().
- off: LLAMA_ASYNC_INPUTS=0.

Qwen3.8-27B UD-Q4_K_XL, MTP n=4, short ctx (6 EN/PL prompts, T=1), host timers:
step 32.20 -> 31.89 ms (target launch 592 -> 376 us, catch-up launch 300 ->
190 us); MTP draft chain set_inputs 193 -> 15 us. Greedy md5 (plain + MTP)
equal to 849b69978.
